br>$E_{12} = 133.8$ |\n| $A_{2}$ | $O_{21} = 40$<br>$E_{21} = 27.7$ | $O_{22} = 10$<br>$E_{22} = 22.3$ |\n| $A_{3}$ | $O_{31} = 72$<br>$E_{31} = 83.1$ | $O_{32} = 78$<br>$E_{32} = 66.9$ |\n\nA chi-square test for independence is conducted at the $1%$ significance level with the following null and alternative hypotheses:\n\n- $H_{0}$: The variables $A$ and $B$ are independent\n- $H_{1}$: The variables $A$ and $B$ are not independent\n\nThe table below gives the values of $w$ that satisfy $P(W \\ge w) = p$, where $W∼χ^{2}(ν)$.\n\n| $ν∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $6.635$ | $3.841$ | $2.706$ |\n| $2$ | $9.210$ | $5.991$ | $4.605$ |\n| $3$ | $11.345$ | $7.815$ | $6.251$ |\n\nUsing this information, select the options that make the following statements true.\n\nRounded to one decimal place, the test statistic is approximately\n{{field-1}}.\n\nThe number of degrees of freedom for this test is $ν =$ {{field-2}}.\n\nAt the $1%$ significance level, there is {{field-3}} evidence to reject the null hypothesis.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172527 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170800} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170801} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170802}] :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170799} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170804} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170805} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170806} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9" :db/id #edb/ref