ificance level, there is {{field-3}} evidence to reject the null hypothesis.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."}] :knowledge-point/title "Chi-Square Tests for Independence" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050794 :topic/math-academy-id 3317 :topic/title "Chi-Square Tests of Independence and Homogeneity"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171993 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170812} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170813} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170814} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170815}] :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "insufficient" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170817} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sufficient" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170818}] :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170820} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170821} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170822}] :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170819}] :question/math-academy-id "q-252790" :question/problem "A particular feature is being examined across two populations to determine if the distribution of the feature depends on the population. The feature can take three values, $A_{1}$, $A_{2}$, and $A_{3}$.\n\nA sample of $120$ individuals from the first population and $80$ individuals from the second population is carried out. The following contingency table reports the observed frequencies.\n\n|  | $A_{1}$ | $A_{2}$ | $A_{3}$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Population 1 | $O_{11} = 30$ | $O_{12} = 36$ | $O_{13} = 54$ |\n| Population 2 | $O_{21} = 40$ | $O_{22} = 18$ | $O_{23} = 22$ |\n\nA chi-square test for homogeneity is conducted at the $2.5%$ significance level with the following null and alternative hypotheses:\n\n- $H_{0}$: The distribution of the feature is the same across both populations\n- $H_{1}$: The distribution of the feature is not the same across both populations\n\nThe table below gives the values of $w$ that satisfy $P(W \\ge w) = p$, where $W∼χ^{2}(ν)$.\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $2$ | $4.605$ | $5.991$ | $7.378$ | $9.210$ |\n| $3$ | $6.251$ | $7.815$ | $9.348$ | $11.345$ |\n| $4$ | $7.779$ | $9.488$ | $11.143$ | $13.277$ |\n\nUsing this information, select the options that make the following statements true.\n\nRounded to one decimal place, the test statistic is approximately\n{{field-1}}.\n\nThe number of degrees of freedom for this test is $ν =$ {{field-2}}.\n\nAt the $2.5%$ significance level, there is {{field-3}} evidence to reject the null hypothesis.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172529 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170824} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170825} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170826} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170827}] :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :an